{"availability":"available","full":"andor-pierdelacabeza/PySimpleGUI-4-foss","name":"PySimpleGUI-4-foss","description":"Mirror of the last GPL version of PySimpleGUI repository","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":94,"forks":73,"created":"2024-02-15T13:43:03Z","updated":"2024-07-18T17:31:19Z","license":"LGPL-3.0","branch":"foss","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"http://demos.pysimplegui.org/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T04:51:56.837Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T04:51:56.837Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T04:51:56.837Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T04:51:56.837Z","stars":94,"forks":73}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["THIS IS THE LAST GPL VERSION OF PySimpleGUI PySimpleGUI has moved from GPLv3 to a custom license with a subscription model (fine with me) but has deleted all its previous GPL code, making it dissapear from the repository. I'm perfectly fine with looking for an appropiate funding model (and their subscription plans look simple and cheap), but I thing that removing all the GPL code from existence, even doing a force-push to the repository, is a petty move that really undermines the confidence in them. Also, it could leave hanging some users that were pending updates or medifications. Thanks to…","PySimpleGUI is a Python package that enables Python programmers of all levels to create GUIs. You specify your GUI window using a \"layout\" which contains widgets (they're called \"Elements\" in PySimpleGUI). Your layout is used to create a window using one of the 4 supported frameworks to display and interact with your window. Supported frameworks include tkinter, Qt, WxPython, or Remi. The term \"wrapper\" is sometimes used for these kinds of packages.","Your PySimpleGUI code is simpler and shorter than writing directly using the underlying framework because PySimpleGUI implements much of the \"boilerplate code\" for you. Additionally, interfaces are simplified to require as little code as possible to get the desired result. Depending on the program and framework used, a PySimpleGUI program may require 1/2 to 1/10th amount of code to create an identical window using one of the frameworks directly."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/andor-pierdelacabeza/PySimpleGUI-4-foss/blob/foss/readme.md","fingerprint":"b22f37e14fcddf81c32b46a517a4b22b5e5e4080df1a4df9d514eb1812b9dc52","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T04:51:57.172Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T04:51:57.172Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"THIS IS THE LAST GPL VERSION OF PySimpleGUI PySimpleGUI has moved from GPLv3 to a custom license with a subscription model (fine with me) but has deleted all its previous GPL code, making it dissapear from the repository. I'm perfectly fine with looking for an appropiate funding model (and their subscription plans look simple and cheap), but I thing that removing all the GPL code from existence, even doing a force-push to the repository, is a petty move that really undermines the confidence in them. Also, it could leave hanging some users that were pending updates or medifications. Thanks to…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/andor-pierdelacabeza/PySimpleGUI-4-foss/blob/foss/readme.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"b22f37e14fcddf81c32b46a517a4b22b5e5e4080df1a4df9d514eb1812b9dc52","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/andor-pierdelacabeza/PySimpleGUI-4-foss/blob/foss/readme.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T04:51:57.173Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2024-07-18T17:31:19Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/andor-pierdelacabeza/PySimpleGUI-4-foss/blob/foss/readme.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T04:51:57.175Z","hash":"b22f37e14fcddf81c32b46a517a4b22b5e5e4080df1a4df9d514eb1812b9dc52","originalBytes":53083,"storedBytes":53083,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["pysimplegui","window","gui","python","code","using","example","one","some","these","what","been","demo","get","pro